{{also|maxout}}
==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|informal|intransitive}} To [[reach]] the [[limit]] of one's [[capability|capabilities]].
#: {{cot|en|tap out}}
#: {{ux|en|In the bench press, he has '''maxed out''' at 110 kg.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|intransitive}} To reach a [[maximum]] or a point at which no more [[growth]] or [[improvement]] is [[possible]].
#: {{syn|en|top out}}
#: {{ux|en|This machine '''maxes out''' at a 110 kW output.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013  |title=Domesticated Wild Things, and Other Stories |author=Xhenet Aliu |page= 69|ISBN=|passage=Nadja had not thought of the word ''elegant'' since her mother made her model for no real occasion one sequined monstrosity after another at Denise's Bridal Affair, pretending her daughter was a pageanteer and hadn't '''maxed out''' at a B-cup.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|transitive}} To use (something) to the limit of its capabilities.
#: {{cot|en|use up|;|fill up}}
#: {{collocation|en|to '''max out''' one's credit card(s)}}
#: {{ux|en|I've spent all afternoon shopping and '''maxed out''' my credit card.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|US}} To relax.
# {{lb|en|slang|US|prison}} To serve an entire sentence with no early parole, time off for good behavior, etc.

